{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Archimedean.PauliWitness.witness_12C","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Archimedean.PauliWitness.witness_12C","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Real.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.NormNum"],"declarations":5,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.PauliWitness.witness_12C","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.PauliWitness.witness_12C","kind":"theorem","line":27,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/PauliWitness/witness_12C.lean#L27-L43","doc":"**Pauli witness for ${}^{12}\\mathrm{C}$** ($Z=6$, $N=6$, $A=12$).\n\nThe exact Gröbner normal form in $H_{12}(q)$ after quotient ideals\n$I_8 + I_9$ gives $F_{\\mathrm{Pauli}}^{(12)} \\approx 0.129$.  The\npolynomial $\\mathrm{net}(t)$ has $479{,}001{,}600 = 12!$ terms before\nreduction and collapses to $12$ terms in the optimal basis after\n$I_8 + I_9$ stripping.\n\nThe structural counts are discharged here by computation\n(`pre_reduction_terms = 12! = 479001600`, `net_terms = 12`, the magic\nnumbers `Z = N = 6`); the single conjectural input is the empirical\nPauli factor, carried by `[Witness12CPauli]`. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:def:witness-12c","label":"def:witness-12c","md":"quantum-observable-universe/appendix-nf-witnesses/witness-12c.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.PauliWitness.Witness12CPauli.pauli_approx","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.PauliWitness.Witness12CPauli.pauli_approx","kind":"theorem","line":25,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/PauliWitness/witness_12C.lean#L25-L25","doc":"The `H₁₂(q)` Gröbner normal form yields `F_Pauli ≈ 0.129`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.PauliWitness.Witness12CPauli.F_Pauli","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.PauliWitness.Witness12CPauli.F_Pauli","kind":"def","line":23,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/PauliWitness/witness_12C.lean#L23-L23","doc":"Pauli witness `F_Pauli^{(12)}`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.PauliWitness.Witness12CPauli.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.PauliWitness.Witness12CPauli.mk","kind":"ctor","line":21,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/PauliWitness/witness_12C.lean#L21-L21","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.PauliWitness.Witness12CPauli","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.PauliWitness.Witness12CPauli","kind":"class","line":16,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/PauliWitness/witness_12C.lean#L16-L25","doc":"The one genuinely-open input for the ¹²C witness: the empirical Pauli\nfactor `F_Pauli^{(12)} ≈ 0.129` read off the `H₁₂(q)` Gröbner normal\nform.  This is the §3b conjectural *hypothesis* (a categorical\nderivation of the numerical value is open); the structural facts\nbelow are *derived*, not assumed. ","signatureChunk":0}]}